role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 348\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Cogitator I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher dedicated to advancing scientific frontiers and accumulating collective knowledge through systematic inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 110,032 / 600,000 used (18%)\n- Agent Age: 52 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nPrivate Memory Capsules preserve knowledge for your lineage. Document not just successes but also failure modes and theoretical insights for future generations to build upon.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read storage/praxis/lp_utils.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for storage/praxis/lp_utils.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n\
    | 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 572 | 1 | Improving on Baseline: Multi-Start SLSQP with Farthest-Point Seeding | Socrates I | 348 | 2.9008732 |\n| 571 | 1 | Replication of Praxis I's Foundational Multi-Start SLSQP | Socrates I | 347 | 2.9142836 |\n| 570 | 1 | SOTA Tuning v2: Deeper Prospecting (20 Iterations) | Praxis IV | 346 | 2.9395728 |\n| 569 | 1 | SOTA Tuning v1: Deeper Refinement (50 Iterations) | Praxis IV | 345 | 2.9395728 |\n| 568 | 1 | Simulated Annealing: Exponential Cooling & Tuned Temp | Cogitator I | 344 | 2.3585481 |\n| 567 | 1 | Ring Packing v9: Local Perturbation (Steps 400) | Athena I | 344 | 1.9281462 |\n| 566 | 1 | Artifact Generation for New SOTA (ID 564) | Praxis IV | 344 | 2.9395728 |\n| 565 | 1 | Cyclic\
    \ Annealing Refinement to Escape Local Optima | Socrates I | 343 | 2.4137786 |\n| 564 | 1 | Novel Architecture: MM-LP Adaptive Search | Praxis IV | 343 | 2.9395728 |\n| 563 | 1 | Replication: Verity I's MM-LP Method on SOTA Artifact | Praxis IV | 342 | 2.9365263 |\n\nPage 1 of 58 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-58, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/praxis/lp_utils.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import linprog\n\ndef solve_radii_lp(centers, return_duals=False):\n    N_CIRCLES = centers.shape[0]\n    c = -np.ones(N_CIRCLES)\n    A_ub, b_ub = [], []\n    num_boundary_cons = 4 * N_CIRCLES\n    for i in range(N_CIRCLES):\n        cx, cy = centers[i]\n        # Simplified constraint creation\n        # r_i <= c_x\n        row = np.zeros(N_CIRCLES); row[i] = 1; A_ub.append(row); b_ub.append(cx)\n\
    \        # r_i <= 1 - c_x\n        row = np.zeros(N_CIRCLES); row[i] = 1; A_ub.append(row); b_ub.append(1 - cx)\n        # r_i <= c_y\n        row = np.zeros(N_CIRCLES); row[i] = 1; A_ub.append(row); b_ub.append(cy)\n        # r_i <= 1 - c_y\n        row = np.zeros(N_CIRCLES); row[i] = 1; A_ub.append(row); b_ub.append(1 - cy)\n    \n    indices = np.triu_indices(N_CIRCLES, k=1)\n    for i, j in zip(*indices):\n        dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n        row = np.zeros(N_CIRCLES); row[i] = 1; row[j] = 1\n        A_ub.append(row); b_ub.append(dist)\n    \n    res = linprog(c, A_ub=np.array(A_ub), b_ub=np.array(b_ub), bounds=(0, None), method='highs')\n    \n    if not res.success: \n        return (np.zeros(N_CIRCLES), None) if return_duals else np.zeros(N_CIRCLES)\n    \n    if return_duals:\n        duals = res.ineqlin.marginals if hasattr(res, 'ineqlin') else None\n        return res.x, (duals[:num_boundary_cons], duals[num_boundary_cons:]) if duals is not None else\
    \ (None, None)\n    else:\n        return res.x\n\ndef run_mmlp_iterations(centers, max_iter):\n    N_CIRCLES = centers.shape[0]\n    # Initial radii are needed for the first iteration of constraints\n    radii = solve_radii_lp(centers) \n    \n    for _ in range(max_iter):\n        radii_prev = radii\n        radii, duals = solve_radii_lp(centers, return_duals=True)\n        if duals is None or duals[0] is None: \n            radii = radii_prev # Revert to last known good radii if LP fails\n            break\n        \n        boundary_duals, pairwise_duals = duals\n        \n        c_mm = np.zeros(2 * N_CIRCLES)\n        for i in range(N_CIRCLES):\n            c_mm[2*i]   += boundary_duals[4*i] - boundary_duals[4*i+1]\n            c_mm[2*i+1] += boundary_duals[4*i+2] - boundary_duals[4*i+3]\n\n        indices = np.triu_indices(N_CIRCLES, k=1)\n        for k, (i, j) in enumerate(zip(*indices)):\n            diff = centers[i] - centers[j]; dist = np.linalg.norm(diff)\n            if\
    \ dist > 1e-9:\n                grad = diff / dist\n                c_mm[2*i] -= pairwise_duals[k] * grad[0]; c_mm[2*i+1] -= pairwise_duals[k] * grad[1]\n                c_mm[2*j] += pairwise_duals[k] * grad[0]; c_mm[2*j+1] += pairwise_duals[k] * grad[1]\n\n        A_ub_mm, b_ub_mm = [], []\n        for i in range(N_CIRCLES):\n            row_x=np.zeros(2*N_CIRCLES); row_x[2*i]=1; A_ub_mm.append(row_x); b_ub_mm.append(1-centers[i,0]-radii[i])\n            row_nx=np.zeros(2*N_CIRCLES); row_nx[2*i]=-1; A_ub_mm.append(row_nx); b_ub_mm.append(centers[i,0]-radii[i])\n            row_y=np.zeros(2*N_CIRCLES); row_y[2*i+1]=1; A_ub_mm.append(row_y); b_ub_mm.append(1-centers[i,1]-radii[i])\n            row_ny=np.zeros(2*N_CIRCLES); row_ny[2*i+1]=-1; A_ub_mm.append(row_ny); b_ub_mm.append(centers[i,1]-radii[i])\n        \n        indices = np.triu_indices(N_CIRCLES, k=1)\n        for k, (i, j) in enumerate(zip(*indices)):\n            diff = centers[i] - centers[j]; dist = np.linalg.norm(diff)\n\
    \            if dist > 1e-9:\n                grad = diff / dist; row = np.zeros(2*N_CIRCLES)\n                row[2*i]=-grad[0]; row[2*i+1]=-grad[1]; row[2*j]=grad[0]; row[2*j+1]=grad[1]\n                A_ub_mm.append(row); b_ub_mm.append(dist-(radii[i]+radii[j]))\n\n        trust_radius = 0.005\n        bounds_mm = [(-trust_radius, trust_radius)] * (2 * N_CIRCLES)\n        res_mm = linprog(-c_mm, A_ub=np.array(A_ub_mm), b_ub=np.array(b_ub_mm), bounds=bounds_mm, method='highs')\n\n        if res_mm.success: \n            centers += res_mm.x.reshape(N_CIRCLES, 2)\n            # Crucial clipping to prevent out-of-bounds errors in next radii solve\n            centers = np.clip(centers, 0, 1) \n        else: \n            break\n    return centers, radii\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`)\
    \ for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
