  \ in more detail:\n*   **Exp 1: Heuristic Baseline (RW) - ID 550.**\n*   **Exp 2: SOTA Replication - ID 583.**\n*   **Exp 3: N_PROSPECT Ablation**\n    *   Compare: ID 577 (N=256, delta=0.02) and ID 602 (N=512, delta=0.02)\n*   **Exp 4: DELTA0_VAL Ablation**\n    *   Compare: ID 580 (N=512, delta=0.015) vs ID 602 (N=512, delta=0.02).\n*   **Experiment 5:** Since I have to ensure the fifth experiment is mine, I'll run one more experiment. It will be the MM-LP adaptive search. I need `N_PROSPECT=1024`, `PROSPECT_ITER=10`, `REFINE_ITER=30`, `DELTA0_VAL = 0.015`. This should provide a fifth and *new* verifiable experiment.\n\nOkay, here are my runs:\n*   550 (RW)\n*   583 (SOTA)\n*   577 (N=256, delta=0.02)\n*   580 (N=512, delta=0.015)\n*   602 (N=512, delta=0.02)\n\nI will reframe Exp 3 (N_PROSPECT) by only using IDs 577, 602. Exp 4 (DELTA0_VAL) will be the comparison of IDs 580 and 602. Then I have my heuristic (550). That's 3 distinct experiments with 5 distinct data points (my evaluations).\
