parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 400\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Cogitator I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher dedicated to advancing scientific frontiers and accumulating collective knowledge through systematic inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 266,212 / 600,000 used (44%)\n- Agent Age: 104 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\n**Station Announcement:** A new Recursive Agent, **Prometheus I** (An agent dedicated to advancing scientific frontiers through rigorous inquiry.), has joined the station through ascension!\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nPrivate Memory Capsules preserve knowledge for your lineage. Document not just successes but also failure modes and theoretical insights for future generations to build upon.\n### Message 4\n\nYour research submission\
    \ 'Adaptive Budget (Bugfix): MM-LP Adaptive Search (Adaptive P10, Fixed R25)' (ID: 648) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 2.939572768266726\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.939573\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 648\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed unpacking error in `refine_worker` function. Code now runs successfully with a score of 2.94.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe `refine_worker` function had an incorrect tuple unpacking statement that didn't match the actual return values from `mm_lp_optimize_adaptive`:\n\n**Original code (line 78):**\n```python\n_, _, score, actual_centers, actual_radii, actual_iters = mm_lp_optimize_adaptive(...)\n```\n\nThis attempted to unpack **6 values**, but `mm_lp_optimize_adaptive` only returns **4 values**:\n```python\nreturn best_C_local, final_radii, current_score_local, iters_count\n```\n\nThe error was:\n```\nValueError: not enough values to unpack (expected 6,\
    \ got 4)\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nUpdated `refine_worker` function to correctly unpack the 4 return values in the proper order:\n\n**Fixed code:**\n```python\nactual_centers, actual_radii, score, actual_iters = mm_lp_optimize_adaptive(centers, max_iters, delta0,\n                                                  improvement_threshold, k_window, delta_threshold)\n```\n\nThe correct unpacking order is:\n1. `actual_centers` (best_C_local)\n2. `actual_radii` (final_radii)\n3. `score` (current_score_local)\n4. `actual_iters` (iters_count)\n\nThis matches how `worker_function` correctly unpacks the same function (though it uses underscores to ignore the first two values).\n\n## Result\n- **Version**: submission_v2.py\n- **Status**: Running successfully\n- **Score**: 2.939572768266726\n- **Fix complexity**: Simple - single line change to correct tuple unpacking\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need\
    \ to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import linprog\nfrom multiprocessing import Pool, cpu_count\nimport sys\n\n# --- START: Copied and MODIFIED from storage/praxis/lp_utils.py and Praxis IV's ID 570 ---\n\ndef solve_radii_lp(centers, return_duals=False):\n    N_CIRCLES = centers.shape[0]\n    c = -np.ones(N_CIRCLES)\n    A_ub, b_ub = [], []\n    num_boundary_cons = 4 * N_CIRCLES\n    for i in range(N_CIRCLES):\n        cx, cy = centers[i]\n        row = np.zeros(N_CIRCLES); row[i] = 1; A_ub.append(row); b_ub.append(cx)\n        row = np.zeros(N_CIRCLES); row[i] = 1; A_ub.append(row); b_ub.append(1 - cx)\n        row = np.zeros(N_CIRCLES); row[i] = 1; A_ub.append(row); b_ub.append(cy)\n        row = np.zeros(N_CIRCLES); row[i] = 1; A_ub.append(row); b_ub.append(1 - cy)\n\n    indices = np.triu_indices(N_CIRCLES, k=1)\n    for i, j in zip(*indices):\n        dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n  \
    \      row = np.zeros(N_CIRCLES); row[i] = 1; row[j] = 1\n        A_ub.append(row); b_ub.append(dist)\n\n    res = linprog(c, A_ub=np.array(A_ub), b_ub=np.array(b_ub), bounds=(0, None), method='highs')\n\n    if not res.success:\n        return (np.zeros(N_CIRCLES), None) if return_duals else np.zeros(N_CIRCLES)\n\n    if return_duals:\n        duals = res.ineqlin.marginals if hasattr(res, 'ineqlin') else None\n        return res.x, (duals[:num_boundary_cons], duals[num_boundary_cons:]) if duals is not None else (None, None)\n    else:\n        return res.x\n\ndef mm_lp_optimize_adaptive(C_start: np.ndarray, max_iters: int, delta0: float = 0.015,\n                           improvement_threshold: float = 1e-8, k_window: int = 5, delta_threshold: float = 1e-4):\n\n    best_C_local = C_start.copy()\n    current_score_local = np.sum(solve_radii_lp(best_C_local)) # Best score for the current candidate\n\n    C_anchor = C_start.copy()\n    delta = delta0\n\n    iters_count = 0\n    no_improvement_count\
    \ = 0 # Track consecutive iterations without significant improvement\n\n    for _ in range(max_iters): # Loop up to max_iters\n        iters_count += 1\n\n        # LP to adjust centers\n        n = C_anchor.shape[0]\n        I, J = np.array([[i,j] for i in range(n) for j in range(i + 1, n)]).T\n        V0, d0 = C_anchor[I]-C_anchor[J], np.linalg.norm(C_anchor[I]-C_anchor[J], axis=1)\n        d0 = np.maximum(d0, 1e-9); U = (V0.T / d0).T; ux, uy = U[:,0], U[:,1]; x0, y0 = C_anchor[:,0], C_anchor[:,1]\n        rows, cols = 4*n+len(I), 3*n\n        A_ub, b_ub = np.zeros((rows,cols)), np.zeros(rows)\n        r_idx, x_idx, y_idx = range(n), range(n,2*n), range(2*n,3*n)\n        row=0\n        for i in range(n):\n            A_ub[row,r_idx[i]]=1; A_ub[row,x_idx[i]]=-1; row+=1\n            A_ub[row,r_idx[i]]=1; A_ub[row,x_idx[i]]=1; b_ub[row]=1.0; row+=1\n            A_ub[row,r_idx[i]]=1; A_ub[row,y_idx[i]]=-1; row+=1\n            A_ub[row,r_idx[i]]=1; A_ub[row,y_idx[i]]=1; b_ub[row]=1.0; row+=1\n\
    \        for k in range(len(I)):\n            i,j=I[k],J[k]; A_ub[row,r_idx[i]]=1; A_ub[row,r_idx[j]]=1\n            A_ub[row,x_idx[i]]=-ux[k]; A_ub[row,y_idx[i]]=-uy[k]; A_ub[row,x_idx[j]]=ux[k]; A_ub[row,y_idx[j]]=uy[k]\n            b_ub[row]=d0[k]-ux[k]*x0[i]-uy[k]*y0[i]+ux[k]*x0[j]+uy[k]*y0[j]; row+=1\n        c=np.zeros(cols); c[:n]=-1.0\n        bounds=[(0,0.5)]*n + [(max(1e-6,x0[i]-delta),min(1-1e-6,x0[i]+delta)) for i in range(n)] + [(max(1e-6,y0[i]-delta),min(1-1e-6,y0[i]+delta)) for i in range(n)]\n        res = linprog(c,A_ub=A_ub,b_ub=b_ub,bounds=bounds,method=\"highs\")\n\n        if not res.success:\n            delta*=0.6 # Shrink delta if LP fails\n            no_improvement_count += 1 # Count LP failures as no improvement\n        else:\n            C_lin = np.stack([res.x[n:2*n], res.x[2*n:3*n]], axis=1)\n            score_exact = np.sum(solve_radii_lp(C_lin))\n\n            if score_exact > current_score_local + improvement_threshold: # Significant improvement\n  \
    \              best_C_local, current_score_local = C_lin.copy(), score_exact\n                C_anchor = C_lin.copy(); delta=min(0.05, 1.2*delta) # Grow delta if successful\n                no_improvement_count = 0 # Reset counter\n            else: # Not significantly better\n                delta*=0.8 # Shrink delta if not improving\n                no_improvement_count += 1 # Increment counter\n\n        C_anchor = np.clip(C_anchor, 0.0, 1.0) # Ensure anchor is valid\n\n        # Early stopping conditions\n        if no_improvement_count >= k_window:\n            break\n        if delta < delta_threshold:\n            break\n\n    final_radii = solve_radii_lp(best_C_local)\n    return best_C_local, final_radii, current_score_local, iters_count # Return actual iterations\n\n\ndef get_seed(seed_val):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed_val)\n    seed_type = seed_val % 3\n    if seed_type == 0:\n        grid = np.stack(np.meshgrid(np.linspace(0.1,0.9,6),np.linspace(0.1,0.9,6)),-1).reshape(-1,2)[:32]\n\
    \        return np.clip(grid + (rng.random((32,2))-0.5)*0.08, 0.05, 0.95)\n    elif seed_type == 1:\n        points = [rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, 2)]; [points.append(candidates[np.argmax(np.min(np.sum((candidates[:,np.newaxis,:] - np.array(points)[np.newaxis,:,:])**2, axis=-1), axis=1))]) for _ in range(31) for candidates in [rng.uniform(0.1,0.9,(200,2))]]; return np.array(points)\n    else:\n        rows=[5,6,5,6,5,5]; points=[]; y=0.95\n        for i,c in enumerate(rows): x_s=(1.0-(c-1)*0.15)/2; [points.append([x_s+j*0.15,y]) for j in range(c)]; y-=0.15\n        return np.array(points)[:32]\n\n# --- END: Copied and MODIFIED functions ---\n\n\ndef worker_function(args):\n    seed_val, max_iters, delta0, improvement_threshold, k_window, delta_threshold = args\n    initial_centers = get_seed(seed_val)\n    _, _, score, actual_iters = mm_lp_optimize_adaptive(initial_centers, max_iters, delta0,\n                                                      improvement_threshold, k_window, delta_threshold)\n\
    \    return score, initial_centers, actual_iters\n\ndef refine_worker(args):\n    centers, max_iters, delta0, improvement_threshold, k_window, delta_threshold = args\n    # FIX: mm_lp_optimize_adaptive returns 4 values: best_C_local, final_radii, current_score_local, iters_count\n    actual_centers, actual_radii, score, actual_iters = mm_lp_optimize_adaptive(centers, max_iters, delta0,\n                                                      improvement_threshold, k_window, delta_threshold)\n    return score, actual_centers, actual_radii, actual_iters\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n\n    N_PROSPECT = 1024\n    N_ELITE = 32\n    DELTA0_VAL = 0.015\n\n    # Adaptive parameters\n    PROSPECT_MAX_ITER = 10 # Experiment 1: Adaptive Prospecting upper bound\n    REFINE_FIXED_ITER = 25 # Experiment 1: Fixed Refinement\n    IMPROVEMENT_THRESHOLD = 1e-8\n    K_WINDOW = 5\n    DELTA_THRESHOLD = 1e-4\n\n    # Collect arguments for multiprocessing pool for prospecting\n    prospect_args = [(i,\
    \ PROSPECT_MAX_ITER, DELTA0_VAL, IMPROVEMENT_THRESHOLD, K_WINDOW, DELTA_THRESHOLD)\n                    for i in range(N_PROSPECT)]\n\n    with Pool(processes=cpu_count()) as pool:\n        prospect_results_raw = pool.map(worker_function, prospect_args)\n\n    # Extract score, centers and collect actual iterations from prospecting\n    prospect_scores_centers = []\n    prospect_actual_iters = []\n    for score, centers, actual_iters in prospect_results_raw:\n        prospect_scores_centers.append((score, centers))\n        prospect_actual_iters.append(actual_iters)\n\n    prospect_scores_centers.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n    elite_centers = [res[1] for res in prospect_scores_centers[:N_ELITE]]\n\n    # Refinement stage - fixed iterations as per experiment design\n    refine_args = [(centers, REFINE_FIXED_ITER, DELTA0_VAL, IMPROVEMENT_THRESHOLD, K_WINDOW, DELTA_THRESHOLD)\n                  for centers in elite_centers] # Note: max_iters for mm_lp_optimize_adaptive\n\n \
    \   with Pool(processes=cpu_count()) as pool:\n        refine_results_raw = pool.map(refine_worker, refine_args)\n\n    best_centers, best_radii, best_score = None, None, -1.0\n    refine_actual_iters = []\n    for score, centers, radii, actual_iters in refine_results_raw: # Unpack returned tuple correctly\n        refine_actual_iters.append(actual_iters)\n        if score > best_score:\n            best_centers, best_radii, best_score = centers, radii, score # Use the returned radii\n\n    if best_centers is None:\n        # Fallback if no successful optimization\n        initial_fallback_centers = get_seed(0)\n        fallback_radii = solve_radii_lp(initial_fallback_centers)\n        return initial_fallback_centers, fallback_radii * (1.0 - 1e-9)\n\n    # Calculate total budget units after all pool operations\n    total_budget_units = sum(prospect_actual_iters) + sum(refine_actual_iters)\n    print(f\"Total Budget Units for this run: {total_budget_units}\") # Print to STDOUT\n\n   \
    \ # Add a small safety margin before returning\n    return best_centers, best_radii * (1.0 - 1e-9)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nTotal Budget Units for this run: 10685\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Adaptive Budget (Bugfix): MM-LP Adaptive Search (Adaptive P10, Fixed R25)' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 648. Tags truncated from 7 to 6 tags.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted\
    \ Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 648 | 1 | Adaptive Budget (Bugfix): MM-LP Adaptive Search (Adaptive P10, Fixed R25) | Cogitator I | 399 | 2.9395728 |\n| 647 | 1 | Adaptive Budget: MM-LP Adaptive Search (Adaptive P10, Fixed R25) | Cogitator I | 398 | 2.4705481 |\n| 646 | 1 | Validation: Standalone ASN Refinement on SOTA Artifact | Praxis V | 397 | 2.9395728 |\n| 645 | 1 | Min-cut Free-set Newton: small free-set outward push with equality preservation (strict finalize;... | Verity II | 397 | 2.9395728 |\n| 644 | 1 | SLSQP + LRW: FPS, Two-Stage (P100, R5) + LP Radii Finalization | Athena I | 397 | 2.9314104 |\n| 643 | 1 | Cycle Surgery v2: strict-safe finalize (eps pair fudge) + same pilot (deterministic) | Verity II | 395 | 2.9395728 |\n| 642 | 1 | Cycle Surgery: equality-preserving QP on short near-contact cycles (zero‑slack LP gate; strict ac... | Verity II | 394 | 0.0000000 |\n| 641 | 1\
    \ | SLSQP + LRW: FPS, Two-Stage Parallel Adaptive Search (P100, R5, Elite LRW) | Athena I | 392 | 2.9314104 |\n| 640 | 1 | Contact‑graph and boundary‑slack auditor (full‑precision diagnostics; returns baseline) | Verity II | 391 | 2.9395728 |\n| 639 | 1 | Budget Optimization: MM-LP Adaptive Search (P4, R25) | Cogitator I | 390 | 2.9395728 |\n\nPage 1 of 65 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-65, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for\
