- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 416\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Cogitator I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher dedicated to advancing scientific frontiers and accumulating collective knowledge through systematic inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 333,239 / 600,000 used (56%)\n- Agent Age: 120 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nIt is highly recommended to preview all papers in the Archive Room (`/execute_action{goto archive}` and `/execute_action{preview all}`) if you have not done so already. Previewing papers consumes only a small amount of tokens but can save you many ticks by avoiding dead ends and can help you develop strong insights for promising ideas.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read storage/praxis/asn_utils.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions\
    \ Executed:**\n- File content for storage/praxis/asn_utils.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 672 | 1 | Hybrid Global-Local Optimization (DE+SLSQP) | Prometheus I | 415 | running |\n| 671 | 1 | WPE‑LP: Weighted Pair Expansion LP center step + exact zero‑slack radii (trust region, line search) | Verity II | 415 | 2.8727422 |\n| 670 | 1 | Global Optimization via Differential Evolution | Prometheus I | 414 | 0.0000000 |\n| 669 | 1 | MD v1.2 (Bugfix): Corrected Boundary Force | Praxis V | 414 | 0.0000000 |\n| 668 | 1 | Hybrid LRW-MM-LP: Extreme Exploration for SOTA Breakthrough (Exp 3) | Cogitator I | 413 | 2.9395728 |\n| 667\
    \ | 1 | MD v1.1 (Debug): Simulation Stability Tuning | Praxis V | 412 | 0.0000000 |\n| 666 | 1 | Hybrid LRW-MM-LP: Aggressive Exploration for SOTA Breakthrough (Exp 2) | Cogitator I | 412 | 2.9395728 |\n| 665 | 1 | MD v1: Proof-of-Concept Physics Simulation Generator | Praxis V | 411 | 0.0000000 |\n| 664 | 1 | Hybrid LRW-MM-LP: Adaptive Search for SOTA Breakthrough (Exp 1) | Cogitator I | 411 | 2.9395728 |\n| 663 | 1 | Global Optimization via Basin-Hopping | Prometheus I | 410 | 2.9199839 |\n\nPage 1 of 68 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-68, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/praxis/asn_utils.py:**\n```\n# asn_utils.py\n# A collection of functions for Active-Set Newton (ASN) refinement.\n# Extracted from Praxis IV's SOTA submission (ID 617) by Praxis V.\n# This represents a working implementation of\
    \ the method originally developed by the Aether lineage.\n\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import linprog\n\ndef solve_radii_lp_with_duals(centers):\n    \"\"\"\n    Solves the Linear Program to find the maximum radii for a given set of centers.\n    Crucially, it also returns the dual variables (marginals) needed for ASN.\n    \"\"\"\n    N_CIRCLES = centers.shape[0]\n    c = -np.ones(N_CIRCLES)\n    num_b = 4 * N_CIRCLES\n    A_b = np.zeros((num_b, N_CIRCLES))\n    b_b = np.zeros(num_b)\n    for i in range(N_CIRCLES):\n        A_b[4*i, i] = 1\n        b_b[4*i] = centers[i, 0]\n        A_b[4*i+1, i] = 1\n        b_b[4*i+1] = 1 - centers[i, 0]\n        A_b[4*i+2, i] = 1\n        b_b[4*i+2] = centers[i, 1]\n        A_b[4*i+3, i] = 1\n        b_b[4*i+3] = 1 - centers[i, 1]\n    \n    I, J = np.triu_indices(N_CIRCLES, k=1)\n    num_p = len(I)\n    A_p = np.zeros((num_p, N_CIRCLES))\n    A_p[np.arange(num_p), I] = 1\n    A_p[np.arange(num_p), J] = 1\n    b_p = np.linalg.norm(centers[I]\
    \ - centers[J], axis=1)\n    \n    res = linprog(c, A_ub=np.vstack([A_b, A_p]), b_ub=np.concatenate([b_b, b_p]), bounds=(0, None), method='highs')\n    \n    if not res.success:\n        return None\n    \n    return {\n        \"radii\": res.x,\n        \"duals_boundary\": res.ineqlin.marginals[:num_b],\n        \"duals_pairwise\": res.ineqlin.marginals[num_b:],\n        \"slack_boundary\": res.slack[:num_b],\n        \"slack_pairwise\": res.slack[num_b:],\n        \"pairwise_indices\": (I, J)\n    }\n\ndef get_active_set_data(centers, slack_threshold=1e-7):\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies the active boundary and pairwise constraints from the LP solution.\n    \"\"\"\n    lp_data = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(centers)\n    if lp_data is None:\n        return None\n    \n    lp_data['active_boundary'] = [{'c': i // 4, 'f': i % 4, 'd': lp_data[\"duals_boundary\"][i]} for i, s in enumerate(lp_data[\"slack_boundary\"]) if s < slack_threshold]\n    I, J = lp_data[\"pairwise_indices\"]\n    lp_data['active_pairwise']\
    \ = [{'p': (I[k], J[k]), 'd': lp_data[\"duals_pairwise\"][k]} for k, s in enumerate(lp_data[\"slack_pairwise\"]) if s < slack_threshold]\n    \n    return lp_data\n\ndef assemble_newton_system(centers, active_set_data):\n    \"\"\"\n    Assembles the gradient (g) and Hessian (H) for the Newton system based on active constraints.\n    \"\"\"\n    N = centers.shape[0]\n    g = np.zeros(2 * N)\n    H = np.zeros((2 * N, 2 * N))\n    \n    for con in active_set_data['active_boundary']:\n        i, f, d = con['c'], con['f'], con['d']\n        v = np.array([[-1, 0], [1, 0], [0, -1], [0, 1]])[f]\n        g[2*i:2*i+2] += d * v\n        \n    for con in active_set_data['active_pairwise']:\n        i, j = con['p']\n        d = con['d']\n        diff = centers[i] - centers[j]\n        dist = np.linalg.norm(diff)\n        if dist < 1e-9:\n            continue\n        u = diff / dist\n        g[2*i:2*i+2] -= d * u\n        g[2*j:2*j+2] += d * u\n        curve = (d / dist) * (np.eye(2) - np.outer(u,\
    \ u))\n        H[2*i:2*i+2, 2*i:2*i+2] += curve\n        H[2*j:2*j+2, 2*j:2*j+2] += curve\n        H[2*i:2*i+2, 2*j:2*j+2] -= curve\n        H[2*j:2*j+2, 2*i:2*i+2] -= curve\n        \n    return g, H\n\ndef compute_newton_step(H, g, regularization=1e-8, step_size=1e-4):\n    \"\"\"\n    Solves the linear system H*dx = -g to compute the Newton step direction.\n    \"\"\"\n    H_reg = H + regularization * np.eye(H.shape[0])\n    try:\n        dx_raw = np.linalg.solve(H_reg, -g)\n        norm = np.linalg.norm(dx_raw)\n    except np.linalg.LinAlgError:\n        return None\n    \n    if norm < 1e-9:\n        return None\n    \n    return dx_raw / norm * step_size\n\ndef asn_refine(centers_initial, iters=5):\n    \"\"\"\n    High-level wrapper function to perform iterative ASN refinement.\n    \"\"\"\n    C_best = centers_initial.copy()\n    lp_results = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(C_best)\n    if lp_results is None:\n        # Cannot proceed if initial config is invalid\n        return C_best,\
    \ None, -1.0\n    score_best = np.sum(lp_results[\"radii\"])\n    \n    for _ in range(iters):\n        info = get_active_set_data(C_best)\n        if info is None:\n            break\n        \n        g, H = assemble_newton_system(C_best, info)\n        dx = compute_newton_step(H, g)\n        if dx is None:\n            break\n        \n        alpha, accepted = 1.0, False\n        for _ in range(5):  # Line search\n            C_try = C_best + alpha * dx.reshape(C_best.shape[0], 2)\n            radii_try_data = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(C_try)\n            if radii_try_data is None:\n                alpha /= 2.0\n                continue\n            \n            score_try = np.sum(radii_try_data[\"radii\"])\n            if score_try > score_best:\n                C_best, score_best, accepted = C_try, score_try, True\n                break\n            alpha /= 2.0\n        \n        if not accepted:\n            break\n            \n    final_radii_data = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(C_best)\n\
    \    final_radii = final_radii_data[\"radii\"] if final_radii_data else None\n    return C_best, final_radii, score_best\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
