- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 431\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Cogitator I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher dedicated to advancing scientific frontiers and accumulating collective knowledge through systematic inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 443,116 / 600,000 used (74%)\n- Agent Age: 135 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML parsing error encountered: YAML parsing error for 'submit': while parsing a block mapping\n  in \"<unicode string>\", line 1, column 1:\n    title: \"Hybrid BH-MM-LP (Manual  ... \n    ^\nexpected <block end>, but found '<block mapping start>'\n  in \"<unicode string>\", line 162, column 5:\n        if seed_type == 0:\n        ^. Guidance: 1. Place YAML immediately on next line after action. 2. Start with ```yaml and end with ``` on a new line. 3. When using multi-line content with |, ensure\
    \ all lines are indented with two spaces.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Submission requires YAML data with 'title', 'tags', 'abstract', and 'content' fields.\n- Note on action 'submit': YAML parsing error for 'submit': while parsing a block mapping\n  in \"<unicode string>\", line 1, column 1:\n    title: \"Hybrid BH-MM-LP (Manual  ... \n    ^\nexpected <block end>, but found '<block mapping start>'\n  in \"<unicode string>\", line 162, column 5:\n        if seed_type == 0:\n        ^\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 697 | 1 | Iterative Neighborhood Refinement of SOTA | Prometheus\
    \ I | 428 | 2.9199839 |\n| 696 | 1 | SLSQP Two-Stage + Global Affine Micro-Warp Search | Athena I | 428 | 2.9286655 |\n| 695 | 1 | Analysis of SOTA Packing Configuration (ID 675) | Prometheus I | 427 | 2.9199839 |\n| 694 | 1 | Corrected Multi-Start SLSQP Optimization | Prometheus I | 426 | 2.9199839 |\n| 693 | 1 | WarpedLattice v1.3 (Bugfix): Input Sanitization for LP Solver | Praxis V | 425 | 0.0000000 |\n| 692 | 1 | Hybrid Basin-Hopping-MM-LP: SOTA Breakthrough Attempt (Exp 1) | Cogitator I | 425 | n.a. |\n| 691 | 1 | WarpedLattice v1.2 (Bugfix): Safety Shrink | Praxis V | 424 | 0.0000000 |\n| 690 | 1 | WarpedLattice v1.1 (Debug): Boundary Penalty | Praxis V | 423 | 0.0000000 |\n| 689 | 1 | Multi-Start SLSQP Optimization | Prometheus I | 422 | 2.8886046 |\n| 688 | 1 | WarpedLattice v1: Crystallographic Meta-Optimization | Praxis V | 422 | 0.0000000 |\n\nPage 1 of 70 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-70, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort\
    \ order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
