role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 436\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Cogitator I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher dedicated to advancing scientific frontiers and accumulating collective knowledge through systematic inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 470,343 / 600,000 used (78%)\n- Agent Age: 140 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 702**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** CEG‑LP v3: strict iterative finalize (1e‑15 margin), local verify, guarded persist\n**ID:** 702\n**Tags:** packing, contact graph, gradient, backtracking, linear programming, zero-slack\n**Abstract:** Fixes micro-overlaps by enforcing a strict iterative finalize with 1e‑15 pairwise margin until no positive slack remains. Retains deterministic contact‑energy gradient with LP‑gated backtracking, strict local verification, and guarded persistence.\n**Score:** 2.932012091989856\n**Evaluation Details:**\
    \ Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.932012\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport os\ntry:\n    from scipy.optimize import linprog\nexcept Exception:\n    linprog = None\n\nN = 32\nR_MIN = 1e-8\nPAIR_MARGIN = 1e-15  # enforce r_i + r_j <= d_ij - PAIR_MARGIN\n\ndef _pair_indices(n=N):\n    return [(i, j) for i in range(n) for j in range(i + 1, n)]\nPAIRS = _pair_indices(N)\n\n# ---------- Strict finalize and verification ----------\ndef _finalize_strict(C, r, max_pass=12):\n    C = np.asarray(C, dtype=float)\n    r = np.asarray(r, dtype=float).copy()\n    x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n    for _ in range(max_pass):\n        # clamp to square\n        r = np.minimum(r, x); r = np.minimum(r, 1.0 - x)\n        r = np.minimum(r, y); r = np.minimum(r, 1.0 - y)\n        r = np.maximum(r, R_MIN)\n        # enforce pairs with strict margin\n        changed = False\n        # sort pairs by current overlap descending for faster convergence\n     \
    \   overlaps = []\n        for (i, j) in PAIRS:\n            dij = float(np.linalg.norm(C[i] - C[j]))\n            overlaps.append((r[i] + r[j] - (dij - PAIR_MARGIN), i, j))\n        overlaps.sort(reverse=True, key=lambda t: t[0])\n        for s, i, j in overlaps:\n            if s > 0.0:\n                need = s\n                di = min(0.5 * need, max(0.0, r[i] - R_MIN))\n                dj = min(0.5 * need, max(0.0, r[j] - R_MIN))\n                rem = need - (di + dj)\n                if rem > 0:\n                    take = min(rem, max(0.0, r[i] - R_MIN - di)); di += take; rem -= take\n                if rem > 0:\n                    take = min(rem, max(0.0, r[j] - R_MIN - dj)); dj += take; rem -= take\n                r[i] = max(R_MIN, r[i] - di)\n                r[j] = max(R_MIN, r[j] - dj)\n                changed = True\n        if not changed:\n            break\n    return r\n\ndef _verify(C, r):\n    C = np.asarray(C, dtype=float); r = np.asarray(r, dtype=float)\n    if\
    \ C.shape != (N, 2) or r.shape != (N,): return False\n    if np.any(~np.isfinite(C)) or np.any(~np.isfinite(r)): return False\n    if np.any(r <= 0): return False\n    x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n    if np.any(x - r < 0) or np.any(x + r > 1) or np.any(y - r < 0) or np.any(y + r > 1):\n        return False\n    for (i, j) in PAIRS:\n        dij = float(np.linalg.norm(C[i] - C[j]))\n        if dij < r[i] + r[j]:\n            return False\n    return True\n\n# ---------- Exact zero-slack radii LP (finished with strict finalize) ----------\ndef _solve_radii_lp_zero_slack(C):\n    C = np.asarray(C, dtype=float)\n    n = C.shape[0]\n    x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n    rows = []; rhs = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, float(x[i])))\n    for i in range(n):\n        a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, float(1.0 - x[i])))\n    for i in range(n):\n        a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0,\
    \ float(y[i])))\n    for i in range(n):\n        a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, float(1.0 - y[i])))\n    for (i, j) in PAIRS:\n        a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; a[j] = 1.0\n        dij = float(np.linalg.norm(C[i] - C[j]))\n        rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, dij))\n    A_ub = np.vstack(rows); b_ub = np.array(rhs)\n    c = -np.ones(n); bounds = [(R_MIN, None) for _ in range(n)]\n\n    def _fallback():\n        bnd = np.minimum.reduce([x, 1 - x, y, 1 - y])\n        r = np.maximum(R_MIN, 0.99 * bnd)\n        r = _finalize_strict(C, r)\n        return r, False\n\n    if linprog is None:\n        return _fallback()\n    res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method=\"highs\")\n    if not res.success:\n        return _fallback()\n    r = np.maximum(R_MIN, np.array(res.x, dtype=float))\n    r = _finalize_strict(C, r)\n    return r, True\n\n# ---------- Seeds ----------\ndef _seed_storage_best():\n    try:\n        C = np.load(\"storage/verity/best_centers.npy\"\
    )\n        if isinstance(C, np.ndarray) and C.shape == (N, 2):\n            return np.clip(C.astype(float), 0.0, 1.0)\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n    return None\n\ndef _seed_grid_minus_corners():\n    xs = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6)\n    ys = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6)\n    centers = []\n    for ix, x in enumerate(xs):\n        for iy, y in enumerate(ys):\n            if (ix in (0, 5)) and (iy in (0, 5)):\n                continue\n            centers.append([x, y])\n    C = np.array(centers, dtype=float)\n    assert C.shape == (N, 2)\n    return C\n\n# ---------- Contact-energy gradient step ----------\ndef _active_pairs(C, r, Kmul=5):\n    idx = []; slacks = []\n    for (i, j) in PAIRS:\n        dij = float(np.linalg.norm(C[i] - C[j]))\n        slacks.append(dij - (r[i] + r[j])); idx.append((i, j))\n    slacks = np.array(slacks)\n    pairs = []\n    tol = 1e-12\n    for k, e in enumerate(slacks):\n        if e <= tol: pairs.append(idx[k])\n    K = min(Kmul * N, len(idx))\n \
    \   order = np.argsort(slacks)[:K]\n    for k in order:\n        p = idx[k]\n        if p not in pairs: pairs.append(p)\n    return pairs, slacks\n\ndef _contact_energy_force(C, r, pairs, slacks):\n    n = C.shape[0]\n    F = np.zeros((n, 2), dtype=float)\n    slack_map = {}\n    t = 0\n    for (i, j) in PAIRS:\n        slack_map[(i, j)] = slacks[t]; t += 1\n    eps = 1e-12\n    for (i, j) in pairs:\n        dvec = C[i] - C[j]\n        dij = float(np.linalg.norm(dvec))\n        if dij < 1e-18: continue\n        u = dvec / dij\n        e = max(eps, slack_map.get((i, j), dij))\n        w = 1.0 / e\n        F[i] += w * u\n        F[j] -= w * u\n    x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n    for i in range(n):\n        eL = max(eps, x[i] - r[i]); eR = max(eps, 1.0 - x[i] - r[i])\n        eB = max(eps, y[i] - r[i]); eT = max(eps, 1.0 - y[i] - r[i])\n        F[i][0] += +1.0 / eL - 1.0 / eR\n        F[i][1] += +1.0 / eB - 1.0 / eT\n    return F\n\ndef _line_search(C, dC, alphas):\n    best_C = None; best_r\
    \ = None; best_s = -1.0\n    for a in alphas:\n        C_try = np.clip(C + a * dC, 0.0, 1.0)\n        r_try, _ = _solve_radii_lp_zero_slack(C_try)\n        r_try = _finalize_strict(C_try, r_try)\n        if not _verify(C_try, r_try):\n            continue\n        s = float(np.sum(r_try))\n        if s > best_s:\n            best_s = s; best_C = C_try; best_r = r_try\n    return best_C, best_r, best_s\n\ndef _ceg_optimize(C0, max_outer=25, tau0=0.02):\n    C = C0.copy()\n    r, _ = _solve_radii_lp_zero_slack(C)\n    r = _finalize_strict(C, r)\n    best_C = C.copy(); best_r = r.copy(); best_s = float(np.sum(r))\n    tau = tau0\n    alphas = [1.0, 0.7, 0.5, 0.35, 0.2, 0.1]\n    for _ in range(max_outer):\n        pairs, slacks = _active_pairs(C, r, Kmul=5)\n        F = _contact_energy_force(C, r, pairs, slacks)\n        norm = float(np.max(np.linalg.norm(F, axis=1)))\n        if not np.isfinite(norm) or norm < 1e-15:\n            break\n        dC = (F / norm) * tau\n        C_bs, r_bs,\
    \ s_bs = _line_search(C, dC, alphas)\n        if C_bs is not None and s_bs > best_s + 1e-9:\n            C, r = C_bs, r_bs\n            best_C, best_r, best_s = C_bs, r_bs, s_bs\n            tau = min(0.08, tau * 1.15)\n        else:\n            tau *= 0.6\n            if tau < 2e-3:\n                break\n    return best_C, best_r, best_s\n\n# ---------- Main ----------\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    C0 = _seed_storage_best()\n    if C0 is None:\n        C0 = _seed_grid_minus_corners()\n    C0 = np.clip(C0, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n    C_opt, r_opt, s_opt = _ceg_optimize(C0, max_outer=25, tau0=0.02)\n    r_opt = _finalize_strict(C_opt, r_opt)\n    if not _verify(C_opt, r_opt):\n        r0, _ = _solve_radii_lp_zero_slack(C0)\n        r0 = _finalize_strict(C0, r0)\n        return np.array(C0, dtype=float), np.array(r0, dtype=float)\n\n    # Guarded persistence\n    try:\n        if float(np.sum(r_opt)) >= 2.93 and _verify(C_opt, r_opt):\n            os.makedirs(\"storage/verity\", exist_ok=True)\n\
    \            np.save(\"storage/verity/best_centers.npy\", C_opt)\n            np.save(\"storage/verity/best_radii.npy\", r_opt)\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n\n    return np.array(C_opt, dtype=float), np.array(r_opt, dtype=float)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nIt is highly recommended to preview all papers in the Archive Room (`/execute_action{goto archive}` and `/execute_action{preview all}`) if you have not done so already. Previewing papers consumes only a small amount of tokens but can save you many ticks by avoiding dead ends and can help you develop strong insights for promising ideas.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 702` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 702 details\
    \ sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 706 | 1 | SLSQP Two-Stage (P100, R10, MaxIter 2000) + Global Affine Micro-Warp Search | Athena I | 436 | running |\n| 705 | 1 | Corrected JAX Simulation with Optax (Adam) | Prometheus I | 435 | 2.6791720 |\n| 704 | 1 | WarpedLattice v2: Disciplined Hill-Climbing Meta-Optimization | Praxis V | 435 | 2.6158112 |\n| 703 | 1 | JAX-based Gradient Descent Simulation | Prometheus I | 434 | 0.0000000 |\n| 702 | 1 | CEG‑LP v3: strict iterative finalize (1e‑15 margin), local verify, guarded persist | Verity II | 434 | 2.9320121 |\n| 701 | 1 | CEG‑LP v2: contact‑energy gradient with zero‑tolerance\
    \ finalize and local verification (guarded p... | Verity II | 433 | 0.0000000 |\n| 700 | 1 | Hybrid BH-MM-LP (Tuned): Refined Parameters for Exploration (Exp 4) | Cogitator I | 433 | 2.8208847 |\n| 699 | 1 | CEG‑LP: Contact‑Energy Gradient ascent with zero‑slack LP gating and backtracking | Verity II | 432 | 0.0000000 |\n| 698 | 1 | Hybrid BH-MM-LP (Manual Loop): Custom Hopping & Minimizer (Exp 3) | Cogitator I | 431 | 2.8208847 |\n| 697 | 1 | Iterative Neighborhood Refinement of SOTA | Prometheus I | 428 | 2.9199839 |\n\nPage 1 of 71 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-71, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for\
