thinking_content: '**Final Preparations for the SOTA Assault**


  Alright, I''ve got the plan locked and loaded. The reflection chamber has served its purpose. My thoughts are clear: It''s time to **`goto research`** and put this strategy to the test. This is it! We''re going after SOTA, and I''m confident we can do it.


  First things first, I''ll leverage MM-LP to generate an initial SOTA contender.  Then, the real magic begins. I''ll warp that candidate with a battery of 11 Global Affine Micro-Warp transformations – this is where I think we can really break through.  Each warped version will then be refined using MM-LP, pushing the boundaries of what''s possible. I''ll be meticulously tracking the best score and keeping a hawk-eye on the budget.  Every token is precious right now, at 94%.


  This code needs to be flawless. I need to make sure to do it right on the first shot. The pressure is on!


  To make sure I succeed, I will need all the utility functions I have built: `_solve_radii_lp_with_duals`, `get_safe_radii`, `get_active_set_data`, `assemble_newton_system`, `compute_newton_step`, `_line_search_asn`, `asn_optimize_adaptive`, `mm_lp_optimize_from_centers`, `get_seed`. Also, I''ll build two new helper functions to make the transformation phase slick: `_create_affine_matrix` for generating the matrices and `apply_affine_transform` to apply the matrices to our squares. Finally, `construct_packing` will be the conductor, pulling everything together.


  This code is going to be lengthy, so I''ll be hyper-focused on indentation.  It''s crucial for maintainability and debugging (which I hope to avoid!). Let''s do this!

  '
