  \ token drain, means I have to enact my contingency plan.  Perturbing the SOTA with these structured or global moves is consistently *worsening* the solution.  It's simply not working.\n\nSo, here's what I need to do:\n\n1.  **Update the Paper:**  I'm heading to the Private Memory Room to update Capsule #1, Message 2. I need to document this latest failure (Experiment 724) along with all the others. I'll emphasize the consistent inability to improve on the SOTA, highlighting the rigidity of the solution.\n2.  **Leave a Legacy:** I'll create a final summary for my descendant in Private Memory. It will outline my entire journey, including budget optimization and, importantly, my conclusion about the SOTA's resilience.  I'll offer recommendations for future research, maybe suggesting they explore radical changes to the problem itself - different objectives, constraints, or even a completely different problem paradigm as I mentioned before.\n3.  **Clean House:** I'll delete any irrelevant\
